content:
{
  "tool": "image_gen",
  "prompts": {
    "trainPrompt": "Use case: identity-preserve. Produce a production 2D battle animation sprite atlas on truly transparent background. Reference is the toy-room original illustrated sprite atlas: reproduce EXACTLY the blue/red/yellow locomotive with green wagon in that image, same painted shaded textured technique, palette, proportions and artist-like finish. No redesign, no pixel-art style change. Subject faces right. Uniform grid SIX columns by SEVEN rows, each cell same size, generous transparent padding no overlap, consistent baseline and camera, no labels no text no room background. Each row is six DISTINCT successive animation drawings, not duplicated static poses or translated frozen copies. Row1 Idle subtle mechanical settling; row2 Walk wheels and connecting rods rotate visibly through six phases, body bob; row3 Steam Blast warm steam builds and vents forward middle-distance over six phases then recovers, wheel mechanics consistent; row4 Front Charge short frontal charge crouch/compression acceleration thrust braking recovery, independently redrawn posture and rods; row5 Hit compress/recoil/recover; row6 Death wobble tilt collapse settle six phases; row7 Walk alternate cycle visibly distinct wheel/rod phases. Keep exact original locomotive identity AND green attached wagon all frames, no face or arms added. Every moving element progresses visually. Deliver usable individual frames with clean transparent gaps. No extra attacks. High resolution atlas 1536x1792 or similar six-by-seven geometry.",
    "robotPrompt": "Use case: identity-preserve. Production animation atlas of the EXACT illustrated retro tin toy robot in reference image1, same proportions, turquoise teal painted cylindrical metal torso, orange/yellow trim, orange feet/hands, square head with two yellow eyes and antenna. Image2 provides the game's hand-painted rendering technique and palette. Transparent background. Fixed right-facing three-quarter side view, no redesign, consistent scale and baseline. SIX columns SIX rows uniform cells, no labels no text no border. Each cell separately redrawn successive pose, not a frozen sprite moved or repeated. Row1 Idle breathing mechanical settling six unique poses; Row2 Walk six sequential alternating legs stepping and swinging arms with distinct silhouette; Row3 Laser Beam six poses windup lean aim straight beam forward firing dissipating recovery, coherent robot anatomy; Row4 Rocket Punch six poses draw back arm, thrust, fist detaches fires forward on short visible mechanical extension, retract catch recovery, do not invent explosion; Row5 Hit six poses recoil compress stumble recover; Row6 Death six phases stagger knees buckle collapse final inert robot. All six frames each row distinctly progressive. Preserve original warm shaded painterly toy texture and identity, no modern robot design, no pixel art, no duplicated frames, truly transparent background. Generous uniform cells including projectile reach.",
    "bearPrompt": "Use case: identity-preserve. Production battle sprite atlas on genuinely transparent background of EXACT original brown plush teddy bear with red-orange bowtie from the provided toy-room atlas. Keep warm fuzzy hand-painted shaded 2D illustration texture, round ears, tan muzzle, black eyes, tan paw pads, round belly, short limbs, original palette and proportions, do not change artist/style to pixel art or 3D. Right-facing three-quarter view. SIX columns by EIGHT rows uniform cells consistent scale, generous clear padding and foot baseline, no text labels borders or scenery. SIX separately redrawn sequential animation phases per row, distinct silhouettes progressing rather than frozen translated sprites. Row1 Idle six subtle breathing/head/arm phases. Row2 Walk alternating heavy plush steps and arm sway six clear poses. Row3 Bear Hug short-range reach: prepare/open arms/reach forward/close embrace/release/recover. Row4 Belly Charge heavy charge: compress/lean belly forward/drive heavy steps/brake/recoil/recover. Row5 Toy Leap: crouch/launch/rise/apex/descending/impact compression; body's elevation visible WITH pose change each stage. Row6 Hit recoil stumble compress recover six phases. Row7 Enrage: six swelling angry determined posture phases with clenched plush paws, changing expression and arms, NO new weapons, no aura palette changes or new attack. Row8 Death stagger/kneel/collapse/slump/settle/rest different poses. Only the approved three attacks. Preserve teddy identity in every frame. Enough padding for leap and hug, no clipping. Frames animation-ready chronological left-to-right.",
    "dinosaurPrompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Create new small toy dinosaur identity specifically matching the existing toy-room artist's hand-painted shaded textured 2D illustration technique, soft warm toy materials, muted turquoise/green/ochre/red accents from reference original train/toys; no pixel art, no photorealistic or 3D render style. A simple friendly rounded toy dinosaur short limbs, rounded muzzle, stout body, little tail, unarmed; consistent identity/proportions throughout, no dragon horns wings or accessories. Production battle animation atlas on genuine transparent background. SIX columns SIX rows, uniform cells generous padding no overlapping sprites, facing right side three-quarter view, consistent scale and foot baseline, NO text labels or backgrounds. Six sequential separately redrawn distinctly changing poses per row, never frozen translated or duplicated frames. Row1 Idle six subtle body breathing/head/tail variations. Row2 Walk clear six alternating footstep/tail/arm phases with body bob. Row3 Bite short bite: prepare lean/open mouth/lunge short distance/snap mouth shut/recoil/recover, no projectile. Row4 Rush rapid charge: crouch lean forward/run step1/runstep2 braking recover, animated limbs not frozen sliding. Row5 Hit six recoil/stumble/compress/recover poses. Row6 Death wobble/kneel/fall onto side/tail settles/head settles/inert final, six visibly progressive drawings. Only Bite and Rush attacks. Preserve SAME dinosaur model and warm painterly game art in all 36 frames. No palette shift during hit/death.",
    "robotCorrectionPrompt": "Edit this exact robot sprite atlas, preserving robot design, painterly style, turquoise/orange/gold palette and every animation's pose progression. Fix ONLY technical cell isolation and missing robot: SIX columns SIX rows, equal rectangular cells, generous fully transparent padding around every complete sprite. Each cell includes the WHOLE robot including antenna and feet. Row4 column4 currently only fist: must include robot in extended-arm firing pose. Shorten laser graphic and extendable fist/cable enough that EACH frame's complete artwork is confined to its OWN cell with at least 16px transparent padding, NO touching or connecting with adjacent frames. No duplicated poses. Keep row order Idle Walk LaserBeam RocketPunch Hit Death. No new attacks or glow effects added. Every limb step, recoil and death must retain distinct progressive poses. Right-facing orientation throughout, fixed character height and baseline. Recompose on larger transparent canvas with roomy uniform cells, no grid lines/text. Transparent background required.",
    "dinosaurCorrectionPrompt": "Edit existing dinosaur animation sheet ONLY to fix clipping and spacing. Preserve EXACT same dinosaur identity, warm hand-painted illustration style, teal body/yellow muzzle/red rounded dorsal bumps, proportions and ALL SIX rows of progressive animation. Six columns six rows. Add generous transparent spacing and margin around each complete frame, at least 20 px on every side. Last column currently clipped at rightedge must be fully reconstructed (whole muzzle, tail, feet). Each complete character must be wholly inside its own equal cell; no row/column overlaps, no cut parts. Uniform scale/baseline. Every successive walk/bite/rush/hit/death must retain clearly changing anatomy poses; no repeated frozen sprites. Rows Idle Walk Bite Rush Hit Death unchanged, no new actions. Transparently padded sprite atlas NO grid lines NO text NO backgrounds.",
    "robotPunchPrompt": "Use case: identity-preserve. Create ONLY Rocket Punch animation of EXACT robot in reference: teal tin toy, square yellow face, orange hands/feet, gold key antenna, warm hand-painted shaded 2D technique. SIX complete frames arranged THREE columns TWO rows. Equal roomy cells, big transparent margins, no text. EVERY cell contains entire robot, never fist-only. Six successive drawings: 1 windup retract forearm; 2 launch arm forward; 3 fist fired forward on short extendable linkage whole robot still visible; 4 fully extended fist maximum reach whole robot leaning shoulder braced; 5 retract fist robot recoiling; 6 recover arm down. Distinct articulated body poses each frame. Rocket Punch only, no explosions. Fist/linkage and robot entirely inside each cell separated from neighboring frames by at least 30px transparent gutter. Same anatomy palette proportions reference. Transparent background. Extended art maximum twice standing body width. Right-facing."
  }
}
